  "id": "electrical-transcranial-stimulation",
  "term": "electrical transcranial stimulation",
  "definition": "Electrical transcranial stimulation is a low-current method that applies electricity through electrodes on the scalp to influence activity in the brain’s outer tissues. The amount of current that reaches the cortex can vary greatly between people and also depends on electrode size and placement, with skull bone differences contributing to this variability.",
